Changes in v6:
- on RX-queue dma_alloc failure, free the buffer-list page before
  cleanup so cleanup does not dma_unmap_single() an address that was
  never mapped
- unmap RX filter/buffer lists by CPU pointer, not dma_addr==0
- double-free/stale-unmap guards named in body; v5
  dma=0-on-map-error unchanged; not a standalone Fixes: tag (helper
  refactor + reopen path)
- debug fmt %u for unsigned num_rx_queues in alloc/cleanup helpers
- pool-fail TX LTB shared-i leak predates helper extract; tip
  fixed in P04 (pool helper no longer consumes i) + P06 (TX unwind). No
  change on P03.
- post-register pool-fail without h_free_logical_lan predates
  this patch. Series tip fixes ordering in P06 (h_free before pool DMA
  on open-fail via out_unregister_lan) and P07 (pools before
  register_rx_queues; post-register errors funnel through
  free_all_queues). No change on P03.
- NULL buffer_list after cleanup — opened gate at tip in P05; no
  change on P03 (hang sentence + no standalone Fixes in P05)

Changes in v5:
- On filter_list DMA map failure: free_page and zero filter_list_dma so
  a later free path cannot dma_unmap the DMA_MAPPING_ERROR sentinel
  (match buffer_list_dma convention). Closes reopen->ifdown WARN path
  after set_csum/set_tso/change_mtu/pool_store close+open while running
  - v4 left the sentinel
- Call out rc = -ENOMEM before the TX LTB loop after RX helper extract
  (already in v4; still required so allocate_tx_ltb failure returns a
  useful errno)
